+  - Studio and runtime typecheck cleanly.
+  - The auth-guard audit finds 0 problems.
+- **New browser suite** `scripts/oct07-review-test.mjs` (`ONLY=<section>` runs one section) passes. It covers:
+  - every workbook item, through the Studio's own controls and the runtime preview;
+  - the conflict cases, against a mocked draft endpoint that applies the database's revision guard;
+  - no console errors.
+- **Mutation checks: 49 / 49 caught.**
+  - 25 in the engine and schema. One mutation broke the build on the first pass, so I rewrote it to build; it is caught.
+  - 5 in the Studio library.
+  - 19 in the browser, across the renderer, the Studio panels, the store, the variant registry and the CSS-driven layout.
+- **Full browser corpus:** 128 suites, 117 pass. The 11 failures were triaged:
+  - **Need a Postgres or `pg` module this sandbox lacks (4):** auth-collaboration, listfill-allocation, lock-concurrency, version-scoped-export.
+  - **Fail with the same message as the baseline (6):** ai-conversation (`rs-probe`), billing (402), dashboard-outage (6/7), picker-taxonomy (Percentage Slider), qa-fixes (emoji default 10), quality (`null.y`).
+  - **Intermittent (1):** media-consolidation passed 4 of 6 runs. The cause was the suite's own race: `$$eval` queries in one round trip and measures in another, and a Live View redraw in between detached the images. The suite now measures again until the elements are attached, and it passes.
+- **Suites fixed to start a fresh respondent:** p0-runtime-contract and tester-fixes failed on every earlier run. The preview resumes its tab's last position, and both suites reused one survey id across scenarios. They now clear the preview's tab state between scenarios, and both pass.
